lesson: 243
title: British coins and notes
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: In Britain a pound is worth 100 pence, written 100p, and a five-pound note is often called a fiver.
explain: To find the change in pence, turn the fiver into pence, find what everything costs in pence, and take it away.
explain: Two ice lollies at 85p cost 170p; from a fiver, which is 500p, the change is 500 - 170 = 330p.
vars: a=name b=name k=2..5 c=4..19 z=2..9
let: p = c * 5
let: cost = k * p
need: cost < 500
answer: 500 - cost
exercise: {a} buys {k} ice lollies at {p}p each and pays with a fiver. How much change does {a.he} get in pence?
exercise: A comic costs {p}p. {a} buys {k} comics and hands over a fiver. How many pence of change does {a.he} receive?
exercise: At the corner shop in Leeds, {a} buys {k} bags of crisps at {p}p a bag. {a.He} pays with a fiver. How many pence come back?
exercise: {a} has a fiver and spends some of it on {k} pencils at {p}p each. How many pence are left?
exercise: Mum gives {a} a fiver for {k} bread rolls at {p}p each. How much change, in pence, does {a} bring home?
exercise: {k} chocolate bars at {p}p each, paid with a fiver. how many p change
exercise: {a} got {k} fizzy drinks at {p+5}p, sorry {p}p each, gave the lady a fiver. change in pence?
exercise: {a} bought {k} packs of football stickers {p}p each innit, paid with a fiver. how much change in p
exercise: {b} says a fiver minus {k} doughnuts at {p}p leaves {500-p}p. nah that's wrong, what's the proper change in pence
exercise: at the chippy, {k} battered sausages at {p}p each, paid a fiver, queue was out the door. pence back?
exercise: {a} breaks a fiver on {k} sherbet dips at {p}p a go. how much {a.he} got left in pence
test: How many pence should come back from a fiver after buying {k} birthday cards at {p}p apiece?
test: {a} hands the newsagent a fiver for {k} magazines priced at {p}p. What change is due in pence?
test: With a fiver in {a.his} pocket, {a} pays for {k} bus tickets at {p}p each. What remains, in pence?
test: {a} buys {k} apples at {p}p each with a fiver, while {b} spends {z} pounds on a scarf. How many pence of change does {a} get?
test: {k} jam tarts {p}p each, gave a fiver. what change in p
test: me nan gave me a fiver, got {k} lollies at {p}p each, how many pence left over
exam: Determine, in pence, the change due to a purchaser who tenders a five-pound note in respect of {k.words} articles priced at {p} pence per article.
exam: It is given that {a}, being in possession of a fiver, subsequently acquires {k} comics at {p}p each. Ascertain the residual sum in pence.
exam: A quantity of {k} ice lollies, each priced at {p}p, having been paid for with a single five-pound note, state the change to be returned, expressed in pence.
exam: Whereas a fiver is surrendered at the till and goods to the value of {k} times {p}p are received, compute the balance owing to the customer in pence.
exercise: {a}'s nan has gone to a better place, and {a} was given the fiver from her purse. {a.He} buys {k} ice lollies at {p}p each with it. How many pence of change does {a.he} get?
exercise: mum's feeling the pinch so it's one fiver and that's your lot. {k} comics at {p}p each, sod it, how much change in pence?
test: {a} told a porky: {a.he} said the {k} chocolate bars cost the whole fiver, but each was only {p}p. How much change, in pence, did {a.he} keep quiet about?
